> group. The thing I don’t understand is if I have stat = "identity" anyway
> why does ggplot plot proportions instead of the numbers when I remove the
> formatter?

Because you used position="fill" which the documentation says is used
to "Stack overlapping objects on top of one another, and *standardise
have equal height*" (emphasis mine). Maybe you want position="stack"

Can anyone help me in getting rid of the % signs next to the
> numbers please?

If you don't want % signs, don't use the percent formatter!

