All,

How does one label the geoms created by stat_summary (and not the data itself):

x <- data.frame(a=factor(c(rep(1:5, each=30), rep(6:10, each=70))), b=rnorm(500))

b<-ggplot(x, aes(a, b)) +
     geom_boxplot(alpha=0, colour="darkgreen", size=0.8, outlier.colour='NA') +
     geom_jitter(position=position_jitter(w=0.15), shape=1, col='red')

b + geom_text()

Alternatively, is there a way to generate a legend that indicates the values of the means in this case? Preferrably with a legend title that indicates the summaries are means (and not medians, actual data, etc.)?

Usually, I find that figuring stuff like this out on my own can be rewarding in that it's a learning experience. However, in this case, I think I've exhausted the possible benefits of trying to figure it out on my own. Thanks again to the ggplot2 for its help.

Adam Loveland

