> How does one label the geoms created by stat_summary (and not the data itself):

Seems like you've done that with color already so I'm not certain exactly what you're after.  Do you really want to label your entire boxplots as being "summary" data?

>
> Alternatively, is there a way to generate a legend that indicates the values of the means in this case? Preferrably with a legend title that indicates the summaries are means (and not medians, actual data, etc.)?

I think what you might be after is a summary table on the graph. I'm pretty sure you can do this, but it's been ages since I've seen anything about this.  I think Baptiste had some code in this group about a year ago with such things. Search the archive for ways of putting tabular data on the graph. You'll have to compute these yourself of course (ddply would probably be best).

Brandon

